# Rule 02. No raw HTML tags outside the kit

This repo is a Vite + Svelte 5 app. `svelte.config.js` is only the
`@sveltejs/vite-plugin-svelte` compiler config. There is no SvelteKit and no
`src/routes`.

## Paths

- Source root: `src`.
- Primitives: `packages/ui/src/ui`. Import them with the `@/ui` alias from `vite.config.ts`.
- Tag groups: `packages/ui/src/utils/tags.ts` (`TagGroup`, `resolveTag`). Host tags inside
  a primitive are chosen only through `resolveTag`.
- Document frame: `index.html` at the repo root (Vite entry). Skeleton and the
  no-flash theme script only.
- Composition, where raw HTML is forbidden: `src/App.svelte`, `src/blocks/**`,
  `packages/ui/src/patterns/**`, `src/blocks/**`, and any other `*.svelte` file outside `packages/ui/src/ui`.

## Goal

Atoms emit tags. Screens compose atoms. Only `packages/ui/src/ui` knows which host tag
is used for which role.

## Zones

| Zone | Raw HTML |
| --- | --- |
| `packages/ui/src/ui/**` | Allowed. Host markup lives here and only here. |
| `index.html` | Allowed, document skeleton only. |
| Every other `*.svelte` file | Forbidden. Use components imported from `@/ui`, `@/patterns`, or `@/parts`. |

## Rules

1. Composition files contain zero raw HTML elements for layout, typography,
   lists, forms or controls.
2. Allowed markup there is a PascalCase component (`Block`, `Button`, …) plus
   Svelte structure that does not choose a host tag:
   `{#if}`, `{#each}`, `{#await}`, `{#key}`, `{#snippet}`, `{@render}`,
   `{@const}`, `{@attach}`, and the special elements `svelte:window`,
   `svelte:document`, `svelte:body`, `svelte:head`, `svelte:boundary`,
   `svelte:fragment`, `svelte:options`, `svelte:self`.
   Contents of `<svelte:head>` are document metadata, same as `index.html`.
3. Every needed tag is searched in this order:
   1. `packages/ui/src/ui`
   2. the matching `TagGroup` in `packages/ui/src/utils/tags.ts`
   3. if still missing, add and export a new primitive under `packages/ui/src/ui`, then
      use it. Never fall back to a raw tag in a screen.
4. Do not fake one primitive with a chain of utility classes on another.
5. Do not hand-edit generated primitive files (`@ui8kit/codegen`). Change the
   generator input or the kit source instead.

`<svelte:element>` chooses a host tag. It is allowed only in `packages/ui/src/ui`.
`{@html}` is forbidden outside the kit.

## Substitutions

| Instead of raw | Use |
| --- | --- |
| `div` | `Box`, `Stack`, `Group`, `Grid` or `Container` |
| `section`, `article`, `aside`, `header`, `footer`, `main`, `nav`, `figure`, `search` | `Block` with `tag` |
| `p`, `blockquote`, `pre`, `figcaption`, `address` | `Text` |
| `span` and other inline phrasing tags | `Inline` |
| `h1` to `h6` | `Title` |
| `ul`, `ol`, `dl`, `menu` | `List` (or `Stack` with `tag`) |
| `li`, `dt`, `dd` | `ListItem` |
| `form`, `fieldset`, `label`, `legend` | `Form`, `Fieldset`, `Label`, `Legend` |
| `input`, `textarea`, `select` | `Input`, `Textarea`, `Select` |
| `button`, `a` | `Button` (`href` renders the anchor) or `Link` |
| `dialog` | `Dialog` |
| `img`, `picture`, `source` | `Image`, `Picture`, `Source` |
| `table` and its parts | `Table`, `TableHead`, `TableBody`, `TableFoot`, `TableRow`, `TableCell`, `TableHeadCell` |
| `details`, `summary` | `Disclosure`, `Summary` |
| `hr`, `br` | `Separator`, `Break` |
| `svg` and paint nodes | `Icon` |
| card surface | `Card` and `CardHeader`, `CardTitle`, `CardContent`, `CardFooter` |

These names are the components in `packages/ui/src/ui`. Confirm the file before using one.

## Validation

Run `bun run retag` in the app (`apps/<app>`; it calls the retag tool of the workspace tooling). It scans every
`*.svelte` file outside `packages/ui/src/ui` and fails when it finds:

- a lowercase HTML element (`div`, `p`, `span`, `h1`..`h6`, `ul`, `button`,
  `a`, `section`, `main`, `svg`, …);
- `<svelte:element>`, including one whose `this` is a string literal;
- `{@html ...}`.

`<script>`, `<style>`, comments, `{expressions}` and the `<svelte:head>` block
are ignored. `index.html` is not scanned.

The report line is `file:line <tag> → Primitive`. Exit code is non-zero when a
file has more hits than `.project/apps/<app>/retag-baseline.txt`. Optional overrides live
in `retag.config.json` (see `packages/tooling/retag.config.example.json`): `allow`,
`allowTags`, `documentFrame`, `exclude`.
